  [1 Stacks] 2 3 4 5 6 7                                
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ⚠ Take over the repository /srv/repo-example as a     
    local stack folder?                                 
                                                        
  Yes makes the changes listed below.                   
                                                        
    folder: /srv/repo-example                           
    case: local (a repository without a remote, deployed
    as it is)                                           
    owner: qhost, group: qhost, mode: 0755              
    the service can write it: yes                       
    permissions are set: no                             
                                                        
  Changes after yes                                     
    The repository is taken over as a local stack       
    folder.                                             
    No permission changes: the service can write        
    already.                                            
    The folder is added to the systemd drop-in of the   
    service, which restarts once.                       
                                                        
    $ sudo qhost source add --expect-effect             
      sha256:example-effect-for-tests-only-0000000000000
      000000000000000 --yes --output json --            
      /srv/repo-example                                 
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
y yes, do it  n/esc/enter cancel              ↑/↓ scroll
